KG42.register("rules-d90fb95d6abe6162d2a48659",{"id":"16-cooperative_microgrid_incentives::v141-c-R005","paper":"16-cooperative_microgrid_incentives","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R005","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Consumer participation","process_stage":"participation","market_meaning":"Customers at node D may cooperate with the private investor to satisfy their electric and thermal load through cogeneration instead of relying on the VIU. Scope: Customers at node D; participation in Coalition {Private investor, D}. Consumers outside the MG cannot join or block any coalition in the game. Scope: Consumer participation in the modeled cooperative game's coalitions. Condition: Consumers are not part of the MG.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function participation.consumer under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["participation.consumer"],"E":[],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"participation","context_text":"Consumer participation in the modeled cooperative game's coalitions. | Customers at node D; participation in Coalition {Private investor, D}.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e005","v141-b-g02-e007"]},"x":[],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R005-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Customers at node D may cooperate with the private investor to satisfy their electric and thermal load through cogeneration instead of relying on the VIU. Scope: Customers at node D; participation in Coalition {Private investor, D}.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["participation.consumer"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e005"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R005-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Consumers outside the MG cannot join or block any coalition in the game. Scope: Consumer participation in the modeled cooperative game's coalitions. Condition: Consumers are not part of the MG.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["participation.consumer"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e007"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e005","location":{"location_id":"src-43db3c92a3-p04-c1r3__v141-a-M01-participation","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"The utility provides power to the other nodes, whose customers also satisfy their thermal load auton","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Instead of relying on the VIU, customers at node D could cooperate with the private investor to satisfy their electric and thermal load through cogeneration. MG generators would also supply reactive power needed by those consumers on a local basis. The value of Coalition {Private investor, D} is the sum of the private investor’s profit and the surplus of customers representing the MG load component. We assume that the utility can effectively prevent the MG from selling excess power and ancillary services to the grid, while still being required to act as a back-up supplier for microgrid customers."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e007","location":{"location_id":"src-43db3c92a3-p04-c1r4__v141-a-M01-participation","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"p g p payoffs of not just its members, but also other players outside the coalition. For example, a ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"It is worth emphasizing that each coalition has an impact on the payoffs of not just its members, but also other players outside the coalition. For example, a coalition between the private investor and the utility affects the surplus of consumers at node D (who are players in the game but do not join this particular coalition), because they are charged rates equal to the VIU’s average cost, which is affected by its coalition with the private investor. Moreover, parties not participating in the game are also impacted. For example, consumers that are not part of the MG cannot join or block any coalition in the game, but their surplus is affected by price changes induced by each coalition, relative to the case in which the utility serves all customers. We consider impacts on all parties when assessing market efficiency."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":"C explicitly supplied only source-backed unary facts for this function; other graph gaps remain reviewable.","empty_x_reason":"No design-selection or operational decision variable is introduced by this participation rule. The source's participation statements are qualitative coalition-membership conditions; optimization variables such as MG generation, flows, and capacities belong to the separate coalition optimization models and are not within this rule's membership condition.","empty_theta_reason":"No parameter, coefficient, numeric value, threshold, capacity, or price is attached to this participation rule. The supplied source text defines only who may cooperate and that non-MG consumers cannot join or block coalitions; it does not state a parameterized participation criterion."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-clearing","v141-a-M01-coordination","v141-a-M01-participation"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"participation.consumer","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e005","quote":"Instead of relying on the VIU, customers at node D could cooperate with the private investor to satisfy their electric and thermal load through cogeneration."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e007","quote":"consumers that are not part of the MG cannot join or block any coalition in the game"}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"51cf1916cda8122e5a84e423120c468ba47c44a6aafcb904c7564759ce5c4d1b","applicability":"non_mathematical","reason":"This frozen rule is a procedural coalition-participation rule, not a quantitative market mechanism. The unreviewed source evidence states only that customers at node D may cooperate with the private investor in Coalition {Private investor, D}, and that consumers outside the MG cannot join or block any coalition. No participation equation, optimization variable, parameter, coefficient, or graph edge is defined for this rule. The mathematical optimization variables in the paper belong to the coalition optimization/clearing models represented under other rules and are not introduced here.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R005-C001","node_ids":["participation.consumer"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The procedural participation condition applies to participation.consumer. The frozen graph has no edge for this unary participation rule; no edge is invented."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R005-C002","node_ids":["participation.consumer"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The exclusion/non-blocking condition is also scoped to consumer participation and is attached to the same existing participation.consumer node. No graph edge is available or needed for this qualitative statement."}],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
